# Build output
/dacli
/dist/

# MkDocs build output (never commit)
site/
/site/

# Go
*.test
*.out

# Python test and helper imports write bytecode beside the source tree.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# Machine-local agent configuration must stay private and be ignored even when
# native checkout observation runs without HOME or the user's global ignores.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Local text and investigation scratch space. Keep the directory and its usage
# contract in Git; ignore every personal artifact placed inside it.
.scratch/*
!.scratch/README.md

# The repo's own dacli workspace lives on its own ref (dacli-record), not on
# trunk. dacli still manages its own backlog — the ARCHITECTURE § 3 dogfood
# test is unchanged — it is just recorded somewhere that does not fork per
# branch.
#
# It was tracked here until 2026-08-06. Branch-carried workspace records are
# the root of a recurring failure class: a task closed on a task branch is
# invisible on main until its record PR merges, so the loop re-picks finished
# work (issue #382); every worktree carried a stale ~6.5MB shadow of the
# workspace it is supposed to share; and 251 of 429 commits were bookkeeping,
# one message repeated verbatim 61 times.
#
# The history is NOT lost — that is what the record branch is for:
#   git log dacli-record
#   git show dacli-record:.dacli/projects/core/tasks/done/<file>
# and every change made before the untracking stays in trunk's own history.
#
# MIGRATING an existing checkout: the commit that untracked .dacli deletes it
# from the index, so git removes those files from YOUR working tree when you
# pull or switch branches — the workspace looks wiped and `dacli status` fails
# with "no readable config". Nothing is lost; restore it from the record ref:
#
#   git archive origin/dacli-record .dacli | tar -x -C .
#
# (Use `git archive`, not `git checkout dacli-record -- .dacli`: the latter
# stages the files again, re-tracking exactly what this change removed.)
.dacli/
